 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The sky is on her; she glides along,\nShe leads a swan in the water's glow,\nAnd with an air of sweet, old delight,\nA few long-sought outswings she\nWandered and flung them over\nAs far as you can see. - And away\nI flew to make myself a\nGay hallelujah for\nFishing upon this shady river.\nTo-day I came back again to\nThis strange lake, with one little\nSmall boat that floats upon",
